  "statusText": "Closed\nThis project no longer accepts pledges or changes.\nFollow to get updates",
  "rewardData": "Team photograph__$25.00(https://cdn.images.indiegogo.com/productimage/noimage.jpg) | Team photograph and patch__$50.00(https://cdn.images.indiegogo.com/productimage/noimage.jpg) | Segundo Barrio FC shirt__$100.00(https://cdn.images.indiegogo.com/productimage/noimage.jpg) | ",
  "tagTexts": "other | ",
  "shortDescription": "Segundo Barrio Futbol Club is seeking to raise funds to enable it to register as a 501 (c)(3) non profit corporation.",
  "projectStory": "Project story\nCreator\nSimon Chandler\nmore infocontact\nCategory\nLocal Businesses\nTags\nother\nBacking information\nCrowdfunding risks\nlearn more\nWho we are\nSegundo Barrio Futbol Club promotes the development of youth soccer players and teams in El Paso's Segundo Barrio neighborhood. We are committed to the growth of well rounded youth through sportsmanship, teamwork, discipline and fun.\nWe work with at-risk youth in one of the poorest neighborhoods in the country. We currently have two youth teams: Under 10s and under 11s.\nSegundo Barrio Futbol Club is seeking to raise funds to enable us to register as a 501 (c)(3) non profit corporation. \nUp to now we have had to rely on the generosity of individual donors. Obtaining 501 (c)(3) status will allow up to apply for the many grants and other types of financial support that are available for sports programs that work with at-risk youth. \n\n\nWhat We Need & What You Get\nWe need to raise $750 to cover the IRS fee to apply to register as a 501 (c)(3) non profit corporation.\n           Perks are:\n$25: Signed photograph of the team\n$50: Signed photograph of the team plus an embroidered Segundo Barrio Futbol Club patch\n$100: Segundo Barrio Futbol Club shirt\n \nThe Impact\nOnce we obtain 501 (c)(3) non profit corporation status we will be able to apply for grants and other financial support which will enable us to not only strenghten our program but also to expand it.\n\n\nOther Ways You Can Help\nIf you are not able to help out right now please share this information with friends and family who you think may be interested in helping out.",
